{
  "_note": "Massing moves taken from built work, written in the massv2 vocabulary. Every number is a fraction of the parcel's buildable plan and legal height; the executor owns the metres. Each scheme is one decisive move, which is what these offices actually do - the variety is between schemes, not inside them. Precedents are named so the recipe can be checked against the building. Each scheme declares far_target: how much of the allowed floor area its brief actually wants. Filling the cap is one brief among several, and forcing every scheme to it produces the stepped monoculture that follows from a single objective.",
